{
	"nodes": [
		{"id": "title", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": -1650, "width": 1500, "height": 140, "text": "# GuideOps Platform — Architecture & Working Plan\nDrag and edit freely. **Green** = source of truth / built · **Yellow** = rules & decisions · **Red** = duplication to fix · **Purple** = planned work"},

		{"id": "g-claude", "type": "group", "x": -2350, "y": -1350, "width": 800, "height": 1260, "label": "CLAUDE SUBSCRIPTION — the engineering department", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "c1", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": -1280, "width": 700, "height": 180, "text": "## Claude Code = deep-work engineer\nBuilds and audits the platform (repos, refactors, dossiers).\nSame account on laptop + VPS (tmux/SSH) + web sessions.\nNOT a runtime API — subscription cannot power Hermes.", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "c2", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": -1060, "width": 700, "height": 200, "text": "## MCP memory server (PLANNED — highest leverage)\nTiny MCP server on VPS tailnet with 3 tools:\n- `memory_recall` → Hindsight\n- `vault_search` → keyword index\n- `memory_retain` → Hindsight\nEvery Claude Code seat gets platform memory.", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "c3", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": -820, "width": 700, "height": 180, "text": "## CLAUDE.md per repo\nClaude Code's native memory. Rides git → identical on laptop, VPS, cloud sessions, any account.\nProject knowledge + conventions live here.", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "c4", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": -600, "width": 700, "height": 190, "text": "## Session-end hook (PLANNED)\nOn session stop → write durable takeaways through Memory Router into the vault.\nReplaces claude-mem's cross-machine role with infra I own.", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "c5", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": -370, "width": 700, "height": 240, "text": "## claude-mem = per-machine diary only\nSQLite in ~/.claude-mem, one per machine, no sync.\nKeep for `/make-plan` locally.\nCloud sessions have none — never treat as platform memory.\nIn AW it only feeds Atlas dots (read-only).", "color": "3"},

		{"id": "g-aw", "type": "group", "x": -1400, "y": -1350, "width": 1150, "height": 860, "label": "AGENTIC WORKSPACE — the brain (:3001, VPS)", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "a1", "type": "text", "x": -1350, "y": -1280, "width": 520, "height": 160, "text": "**Model Intelligence**\nOpenRouter + Artificial Analysis + models.dev → curated catalog + sanctioned roster agents read."},
		{"id": "a2", "type": "text", "x": -780, "y": -1280, "width": 500, "height": 160, "text": "**Ministry of Experts**\nMixture-of-Agents preset builder → writes moa presets into Hermes config.yaml."},
		{"id": "a3", "type": "text", "x": -1350, "y": -1090, "width": 520, "height": 160, "text": "**Helm — voice remote control**\nZero-LLM intent registry: navigate, theme, kanban ops. Global HUD. Shares Echoes STT/TTS verbatim."},
		{"id": "a4", "type": "text", "x": -780, "y": -1090, "width": 500, "height": 160, "text": "**Echoes — voice conversation**\nStaircase: regex → Helm data → local Ollama → Hermes.\n⚠ No retrieval step yet; `sources: []` is the empty citation slot."},
		{"id": "a5", "type": "text", "x": -1350, "y": -900, "width": 520, "height": 160, "text": "**Second Brain (/atlas)**\nCanvas-2D galaxy of vault + claude-mem + skills. A MAP, not a memory — read-only, feeds no prompts. Ask-box = memory.js recall."},
		{"id": "a6", "type": "text", "x": -780, "y": -900, "width": 500, "height": 160, "text": "**Dream + Sentinel**\nRead-only engines: cost optimization digest · security posture scan → vault."},
		{"id": "a7", "type": "text", "x": -1350, "y": -710, "width": 520, "height": 160, "text": "**Skills (~19 command files)**\ndeep-research, digests, morning-brief, finance pack…\n⚠ Some write vault files directly (ungoverned lane)."},
		{"id": "a8", "type": "text", "x": -780, "y": -710, "width": 500, "height": 160, "text": "**Memory Router → Review Inbox**\nThe governed write lane into the vault (approve/reject → ACL commit). Should be the ONLY write lane."},

		{"id": "g-hermes", "type": "group", "x": -1400, "y": -350, "width": 1150, "height": 620, "label": "HERMES AGENT — runtime (Nous Research, external install)", "color": "5"},
		{"id": "h1", "type": "text", "x": -1350, "y": -280, "width": 520, "height": 210, "text": "**Gateway + adapter**\ntui_gateway JSON-RPC over WebSocket (agentBridge) + hermes CLI (status/control).\nWrapper injects NOTHING into prompts — pull-based by design.", "color": "5"},
		{"id": "h2", "type": "text", "x": -780, "y": -280, "width": 500, "height": 210, "text": "**Toolsets + channels**\n76 built-in toolsets · MCP servers · Telegram / WhatsApp / Discord.\n💳 Needs pay-as-you-go API key (Anthropic or OpenRouter paid-cheap + free fallback).", "color": "5"},
		{"id": "h3", "type": "text", "x": -1350, "y": -30, "width": 1070, "height": 210, "text": "**Built-in memory = sticky notes on the robot**\nSOUL.md (persona; wrapper writes it on persona apply) + MEMORY.md/USER.md (char-capped, Hermes+curator owned, always injected) + state.db (transcripts, FTS) + kanban.db (⚠ third board — mirror or ignore deliberately).\nKeep small: always-on facts only, never an archive.", "color": "3"},

		{"id": "g-aura", "type": "group", "x": 0, "y": -1350, "width": 1150, "height": 590, "label": "AURA — eyes + handbrake", "color": "2"},
		{"id": "u1", "type": "text", "x": 50, "y": -1280, "width": 520, "height": 220, "text": "**Isometric office**\nAgents as robots, fed by free 'postcards' (AgentEvents) — observation without sitting in the request path. Claude Code adapter built; Codex adapter planned; Hermes via AW."},
		{"id": "u2", "type": "text", "x": 620, "y": -1280, "width": 480, "height": 220, "text": "**Kanban — the ONE board**\nPersistence, revisions, GitHub Projects sync. AW's board gets retired; Hermes kanban.db decided deliberately."},
		{"id": "u3", "type": "text", "x": 50, "y": -1020, "width": 520, "height": 220, "text": "**Approvals + guardrails**\npermissions.yaml · tool.ask parks dangerous calls until I approve in the office. The reason AURA exists as a separate trust boundary."},
		{"id": "u4", "type": "text", "x": 620, "y": -1020, "width": 480, "height": 220, "text": "**Vault UI + live graph**\nSQLite FTS5 derived index (rebuildable). Right tool — do NOT add a RAG here."},

		{"id": "g-mem", "type": "group", "x": 0, "y": -620, "width": 1500, "height": 1010, "label": "MEMORY — one corpus, disposable indexes", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "m1", "type": "text", "x": 50, "y": -550, "width": 650, "height": 280, "text": "## 📁 Obsidian vault — SOURCE OF TRUTH\nMarkdown · Syncthing across machines · **add git nightly auto-commit (sync ≠ backup!)**\nOne writer per subfolder: aw/ · memory/ · briefs/ · mine\nFrontmatter contract: type · created · tags · status · project\nStructure: projects/ areas/ study/ notes/ raw/ wiki/\n**Durability test:** delete every index → rebuild from markdown, lose nothing.", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "m2", "type": "text", "x": 750, "y": -550, "width": 700, "height": 280, "text": "## 🧠 Hindsight — agent EXPERIENCE only\nvectorize-io/hindsight · Docker :8888 · embedded Postgres+pgvector · local embeddings · Ollama extraction · zero egress · tailnet-reachable.\nretain = LLM fact-extraction (lossy — wrong for verbatim notes!)\nrecall = vector + BM25 + graph + time, fused (RRF) + reranked\nreflect = synthesized answer across memories\n**Does NOT index the vault — keep it that way.**", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "m3", "type": "text", "x": 50, "y": -230, "width": 650, "height": 190, "text": "**memory.js keyword index**\nDeterministic: score _master-index.md → open 1 best file → 1 best section → ≤1 wikilink hop. No embeddings by benchmarked choice. Serves /api/brain/recall.", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "m4", "type": "text", "x": 750, "y": -230, "width": 700, "height": 190, "text": "## RULE: every fact gets ONE home\nVault = knowledge (mine) · Hindsight = agent experience · claude-mem = Claude Code diary (per machine) · Sticky notes = always-on facts only.\nAll indexes rebuildable; memory follows storage I own, not accounts.", "color": "3"},
		{"id": "m5", "type": "text", "x": 50, "y": 20, "width": 1400, "height": 310, "text": "## ⚠ Duplication debt (from audit 2026-07-19)\n- **4 incompatible 'remember a fact' lanes**: Hindsight · memory.js · claude-mem · Hermes MEMORY.md → collapse to 2 (Hindsight semantic + memory.js deterministic)\n- **3 vault-graph walkers** (Atlas, Echoes graph, memory.js) → extract one shared walker lib\n- **2 vault write lanes** (Router-governed vs direct skill writes) → close the ungoverned one\n- **Hindsight wired twice** (direct HTTP + Hermes provider slot) → keep direct HTTP only\n- **3 kanban boards** → AURA's survives\n- **Nothing injects memory into prompts** — pull-based everywhere; agent must volunteer to ask. Echoes/Helm have zero retrieval today.", "color": "1"},

		{"id": "g-org", "type": "group", "x": 1250, "y": -1350, "width": 780, "height": 590, "label": "ORGBRAIN — 'Guidant AI' (separate product)", "color": "5"},
		{"id": "o1", "type": "text", "x": 1300, "y": -1280, "width": 680, "height": 460, "text": "**Multi-tenant SaaS — scope has held**\nNext.js 16 · Postgres/PGlite + pgvector · Claude tiers (Haiku link / Sonnet copilot / Opus conductor) · Tauri shell · Stripe skeleton.\n\n**The 2nd true RAG:** MiniLM-local or Voyage → pgvector + tsvector, RRF fusion, **permissions enforced inside the SQL**, canSee re-check, audit trace per query, lexical fallback. Reranker built, off by eval verdict.\n\nZero code coupling to Hermes/AW/AURA — by documented choice.\nDebts: no ANN index (brute-force scan), billing skeleton.", "color": "5"},

		{"id": "g-plan", "type": "group", "x": -2350, "y": 550, "width": 3920, "height": 740, "label": "ACTION PLAN — ordered next moves", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "p1", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": 630, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 1 · Git the vault\n- [ ] Init repo + nightly auto-commit\n- [ ] Keep Syncthing for sync; git for history/backup\nFoundation for everything else — Syncthing propagates deletions.", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "p2", "type": "text", "x": -1330, "y": 630, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 2 · MCP memory server ⭐\n- [ ] 3 tools: memory_recall / vault_search / memory_retain\n- [ ] Runs on VPS, reachable over tailnet\n- [ ] Register in Claude Code config on every machine\nMakes the Claude subscription a full citizen of my memory.", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "p3", "type": "text", "x": -360, "y": 630, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 3 · Collapse memory lanes\n- [ ] Vault = knowledge · Hindsight = experience (no vault sync)\n- [ ] claude-mem → Atlas feed only · MEMORY.md → prompt cache\n- [ ] Keep Hindsight direct-HTTP path, drop provider slot\n- [ ] One shared vault-graph walker · close direct skill-writes", "color": "1"},
		{"id": "p4", "type": "text", "x": 610, "y": 630, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 4 · Echoes → Perplexity mode\n- [ ] Insert recall tier (memory.js + Hindsight) before Ollama\n- [ ] Populate the existing sources[] field → citations\n- [ ] Swap Ollama to 3B model (llama3.2:3b) for speed\n- [ ] OpenRouter key: paid-cheap primary, free fallback\nKeep Helm as deterministic tier-0 commands.", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "p5", "type": "text", "x": -2300, "y": 930, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 5 · Claude Code hooks + CLAUDE.md\n- [ ] Session-end hook → takeaways via Memory Router → vault\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md in every active repo\n- [ ] Same account on laptop + VPS + web", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "p6", "type": "text", "x": -1330, "y": 930, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 6 · AURA ↔ AW pairing (steps A→E)\n- [ ] A: pair (6-digit code → token)\n- [ ] B: AgentEvent batches (250ms)\n- [ ] C: retire AW kanban\n- [ ] D: approval gating (the handbrake)\n- [ ] E: optional 3-tool MCP surface (maybe never)", "color": "2"},
		{"id": "p7", "type": "text", "x": -360, "y": 930, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 7 · AURA multi-provider office\n- [ ] Codex adapter (watch session logs → postcards)\n- [ ] Claude Code hooks already built ✓\n- [ ] Hermes robots arrive via AW events (step B)\nNever route models through Hermes just to see them — observe via events, zero token cost.", "color": "2"},
		{"id": "p8", "type": "text", "x": 610, "y": 930, "width": 880, "height": 260, "text": "### 8 · Hygiene\n- [ ] Mark /rag-pipeline skill superseded by Hindsight in docs\n- [ ] Decide Hermes kanban.db: mirror or ignore\n- [ ] No RAG in AURA (FTS5 is correct)\n- [ ] OrgBrain: add ANN index when >1k entities · future AW → /api/ingest push only", "color": "3"}
	],
	"edges": [
		{"id": "e1", "fromNode": "g-aw", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "g-hermes", "toSide": "top", "label": "drives: CLI adapter + WS bridge"},
		{"id": "e2", "fromNode": "g-aw", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "g-aura", "toSide": "left", "label": "AgentEvents → :8311 · pairing token"},
		{"id": "e3", "fromNode": "g-hermes", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "u3", "toSide": "left", "label": "tool.ask → blocks until approved", "color": "2"},
		{"id": "e4", "fromNode": "a8", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "m1", "toSide": "left", "label": "governed write lane (aw/ + memory/)", "color": "4"},
		{"id": "e5", "fromNode": "g-aura", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "m1", "toSide": "top", "label": "briefs/ + FTS5 index", "color": "2"},
		{"id": "e6", "fromNode": "g-claude", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "g-aw", "toSide": "left", "label": "builds + audits everything", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "e7", "fromNode": "c2", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "m2", "toSide": "left", "label": "planned: MCP recall/retain", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "e8", "fromNode": "c4", "fromSide": "right", "toNode": "a8", "toSide": "left", "label": "planned: takeaways → Router", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "e9", "fromNode": "a4", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "m3", "toSide": "top", "label": "planned: recall tier + citations", "color": "6"},
		{"id": "e10", "fromNode": "g-org", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "g-aw", "toSide": "right", "label": "no code link · future: push via /api/ingest", "color": "5"},
		{"id": "e11", "fromNode": "m1", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "m5", "toSide": "top", "label": "indexed 4 ways today", "color": "1"},
		{"id": "e12", "fromNode": "g-claude", "fromSide": "bottom", "toNode": "g-plan", "toSide": "left", "label": "subscription does this work", "color": "6"}
	]
}
